    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "N 331P\nAERO\nVIRGINISLANDS, Corp.\nEMERGENCY INFORMATION CARD\nDOUGLAS DC-3\nYou are flying aboard a DC-3, with a Captain and Crew\nwho are thoroughly trained and experienced. There is little\nlikelihood we will encounter a situation requiring emergency\npreparations but it is a good practice to be aquainted with\nthe safety features we have provided for you on this airplane.\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nFour exits are available for your use. The diagram indi-\ncates the exits. Red arrows indicate hinged windows. The\nblack arrow indicated rear door exit.\nWINDOW EXITS\nSTEP |\nREMOVE PLASTIC\nCOVER\nCARGO\nCARGO\nSTEP 2\nTURN HANDLE\nCLOCKWISE\nSTEP 3\nPUSH WINDOW\nFORWARD AND\nOUT, REMOVE\nCOMPLETELY\nLIFE VEST INSTRUCTIONS\nOTHER SIDE",
      "FOR YOUR INFORMATION\nPORTABLE ELECTRONIC DEVICES\nCertain portable electronic divices\nact like miniature\nbroadcasting stations and may cause interference with\nairborne navigational equipment. Therefore, no person shall\nbe allowed to operate any portable electronic, device on\naircraft in flight. This regulation does not apply to:\n1. Portable Voice Recorders\n2. Hearing Aids\n3. Heart Pacemakers\n4. Electric Shavers\nSEAT BELTS\nMove around as much as you like in the cabin while the seat\nbelt sign is off. We suggest, however, that you keep your seat\nbelt loosely fastened while in your seats. Of course, seat\nbelts must be fastened any time the seat belt sign is on.\nNO SMOKING\nWhen the \"No Smoking\" sign is off, you may smoke ciga-\nrettes while seated anywhere in the cabin. Whenever the \"No\nSmoking\" sign comes on, however, all smokes are to be\nextinguished.\nINSTRUCTIONS FOR USE OF AIRLINE LIFE VEST\n1. Put on over head.\n2. Insert waist strap in buckle.\n3. Pull tight around waist.\n4. Pull down sharply on red plastic knob.\n5. If life jacket becomes too soft place mouthpiece against\nlips and blow.\nDO NOT INFLATE IN CABIN"
    ],
